course: dictionary
lesson: 3957
title: Context clues: furnace
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to choose. Furnace is one of those words. In «Sand is melted with soda and crushed limestone in a furnace hotter than 1000 °C», the clues are melted and hotter, so a furnace must be a very hot fire or oven used to melt things.
explain: Read the words around the word. In «The classroom was a furnace today», there is no oven, so furnace must mean a very hot place. Check it by swapping in the meaning: a very hot place fits the sentence, so you have the right one.
explain: In «The three friends were thrown into a fiery furnace», the word fiery is a clue that the furnace is a place of fire. In North America, furnace can also mean the heater in a house, so when a sentence talks about warming the home, pick that meaning.
fact: A furnace is a very hot enclosed fire or oven used to melt metal, make glass or burn things.
fact: In North America, a furnace is the heater in a house that warms the air or water for the whole home.
fact: A blast furnace melts iron from rock to make steel.
fact: «Hot as a furnace» is a phrase that means very, very hot.
fact: Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego walked unharmed in a fiery furnace, according to the Bible.
exercise: «Sand is melted with soda and crushed limestone in a furnace hotter than 1000 °C.» What is a furnace? | A soft cushion for glass | A cold cupboard for storing sand | A kind of small boat | *A very hot enclosed fire or oven used to melt things
exercise: Mum says, «The furnace in the basement is on, so the house is warm.» In North America, what does furnace mean here? | *The heater that warms the whole home | A cold room under the stairs | A sandy beach | A place where iron is melted
exercise: «The classroom was a furnace today.» What does furnace mean here? | A heap of loose rocks | *A very hot place | A cold cellar full of ice | A type of clear glass
test: «The three friends were thrown into a fiery furnace but were not burnt.» Find and copy the word that tells you the furnace was on fire. | friends | burnt | *fiery | thrown
test: Which phrase means that something is very hot? | *hot as a furnace | cool as a breeze | wet as a rainy day
exam: In «people heat it with carbon in a furnace to pull the oxygen away and get iron», what is the furnace used for? | To grow plants in the classroom | To store books and papers | *To melt iron ore so the oxygen is pulled away and iron is left | To cool down ice for drinks
